# Electric Power Control Method

An electric power control method comprising:

- a **current measuring step**;
- a **command value calculating step**;
- an **operating step**;
- a **determining step**, in which a determination is made as to whether the operation period during which the operating step is performed should be extended to be longer than one cycle of the carrier wave;
- a **first reducing step**, in which the switching operation of the switching elements is reduced during the first half cycle of the carrier wave, beginning at the start timing of the operation period following the change, during which the carrier wave changes monotonically;
- a **comparing step**, in which the slope of the carrier wave is altered during an intermediate period—situated between the first half cycle and the last half cycle of the carrier wave within the operation period following the change—so as to compare the magnitude of the carrier wave with the duty command value, the switching operation of the switching elements being performed in accordance with the result of this comparison; and
- a **second reducing step**, in which the switching operation of the switching elements is reduced during the last half cycle of the carrier wave.
